When I started this project in 2023-24, there was the development loop:

[1]
Understand the code context youself.
Ask GPT questions.
Enter them yourself.

[2]
Then, in 2025 agents came out and the loop changed to:
Ask GPT to fix code.
GPT understands code context.
GPT changes code.
Review changes.


What I have found for the last 2 months of trying to complete this project, is that the new agent loops
is incompatible for complex system development and maitenance. The more power I give to these agents,
in understanding and changing the context themselves, the less I am able to modify and understand the system myself.
In example, I have the entire 100% of the code context in my own brain in the loop #1.
Now in loop 2, I started with 100% of the code context, but as GPT makes changes, I lose that understanding.
I now no longer have the competency to debug and maintain the code. That is human out of the loop.
So, my current conclusion, is that the human must be in the loop to a greater extent beyond just review of changes.
My only hope for completing this project is reverting the last 2 months of changes, and doing it all over myself
with loop [1].
Linus himself states:
VIBE = Very Inefficient But Entertaining
